tain control.\n\nReason:\nPlaying ♦K is the optimal move because: (1) It\'s a strong single card that pressures the landlord to use premium cards or pass, (2) If the landlord passes, control goes to my teammate who can continue the momentum, (3) Playing low cards would likely give the landlord easy control when they\'re dangerously close to winning with only 4 cards, (4) This maximizes our team\'s chance of regaining/maintaining control of the game.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦K"]}'}
